                "content": "## SERRANO & CARPENTER CANAL NEAR VILLA PARK, CALIF.\n\nLOCATION.-Water-stage recorder in SW. 1/4 sec. 13, T. 4 S., R. 9 W., at division box half a mile above mouth of Santiago Creek Canyon and 21/4 miles north- east of Villa Park.\n\nRECORDS AVAILABLE. August, 1920, to September, 1931. EXTREMES.-1920-1931 Maximum mean daily discharge, 16.8 second-feet May 20, 1922; no water is diverted at times.\n\nREMARKS.-Records, good. Canal diverts from Santiago Creek at Point of Rocks. At the division box the flow is divided between John T. Carpenter and lands on the north and south sides of Santiago Creek. During periods of Serrano Water Cos. and is carried through concrete pipe lines to orchard shortage both companies augment their supply by pumping.\n\nDaily and monthly discharge, in second-feet, 1930-31",
